From: Squeezebox RG35XX-H project (boot-progress LEDs)
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] arm64: dts: allwinner: rg35xx-h: heartbeat on status LED
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate (board-specific OOT staging; trivial enough
 to upstream later as a default-trigger one-liner once HW-proven)
Squeezebox-OOT: yes - master copy: platform/rg35xx-h/device-tree/rg35xx-h-leds-oot.dtsi

Bind the heartbeat trigger to the in-tree status LED (PI11) so a booting
kernel shows signs of life before userspace starts. Userspace led.sh
switches the trigger to per-stage patterns once systemd runs.

Validated: patch applies after 0005 with no fuzz; H DTB rebuild is part of
the 0.3.0 image build (fails closed on DT errors). HW gate: observe
heartbeat on the status LED during kernel boot.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/rg35xx-h-leds-oot.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+/*
+ * RG35XX-H status-LED trigger (out-of-tree). Master copy — mirrored verbatim
+ * into the kernel tree by platform/rg35xx-h/kernel/patches/0006 (keep in sync).
+ *
+ * The in-tree board DTS already defines gpio-leds (led-0 power on PI12 with
+ * default-state "on", led-1 status on PI11, both active-high). This override
+ * binds the heartbeat trigger to the STATUS led at probe: a kernel-alive
+ * signal until userspace led.sh takes over with per-stage patterns
+ * (see platform/rg35xx-h/services/led.sh and docs/hardware.md "LEDs").
+ * Needs CONFIG_LEDS_TRIGGER_HEARTBEAT=y (in linux-rg35xx-h-aarch64.conf).
+ */
+
+&{/leds/led-1} {
+	linux,default-trigger = "heartbeat";
+};
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-h.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-h.dts
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dts"
 /* Squeezebox OOT: display pipeline (panel + backlight + enables). */
 #include "rg35xx-h-display-oot.dtsi"
+#include "rg35xx-h-leds-oot.dtsi"
 
 / {
 	model = "Anbernic RG35XX H";
